adjudication.rationale:
In `addGuests.handler.ts`, email sending is wrapped in a try/catch:
```ts
try {
  await sendAddGuestsEmails(evt, guests);
} catch (err) {
  console.log("Error sending AddGuestsEmails");
}
```
The catch block does not rethrow, return an error, or record the actual `err` object; it only prints a generic message. This means failures are effectively swallowed (request still returns success) and there is no structured logging/telemetry nor useful error details captured.
